![Spend vs cost-per-DALY frontier. The horizontal dashed line marks the 1× GDP per capita ICER threshold (R110,000/DALY). All options below this line are cost-effective under the WHO convention.](overall_policy_model_v2_files/figure-html/fig-daly-frontier-1.png){#fig-daly-frontier width=960}
:::
:::


**Interpretation.** Under GBD 2019 weights, every scenario from 1.1 upward falls **below the R110,000/DALY threshold**, confirming cost-effectiveness under the WHO convention. The DALY NMB is larger than the human-capital NMB at the lower spend levels (DALY valuation reflects broader health burden) and converges at higher spend where induced workload dominates. **This result is sensitive to `yll_mean_age_at_death`** — update `yll_per_death_gbd` in the CSV once the StatsSA MACOD age distribution is tabulated; a 10-year shift in mean age changes YLL/death by 10 yr and the DALY NMB by ~R1.1B.



